Load decks of sp_mos6 against ngspice-45, written by ../load.py mos6.
Builds on PATH: ngspice-45 jfngv2gd3zvi5cmr9vrqfhnziipqd09n (source hfvpfb0bgw9819wkb7kzpdaasbd0hd5r, devices/mos6),
VACASK dhxz6l3iac3r2b8n91kcz04a0j3hs4s6 (devices/spice/mos6.va, ngspice-47-159 vadng-pre-48).
Run: `nix develop .#testing -c tests/fixtures/families/load_run.sh mos6`. i(vd) in A, |i(vd)| at 1 GHz for acg/acd.
nom is 27 C, m=1, the control of m3 (27 C, m=3) and of off (80 C, m=3); all give w, l, ad, as, pd, ps, a bulk at -0.5 V,
junctions (cj, cjsw, js) and Meyer capacitances (tox, cgso, cgdo, cgbo). Regions (vgs, vds): cut (0.3, 2), lin (3, 0.2),
sat (1.5, 3).
Oracles (fd.py, last lines): each nominal region's operating point moved 1e-5 V on the gate (base) and the drain
(collector, anode), whose central differences are gm and gds of the DC law, against |i(vd)| at 1 kHz; it holds where
the conductance is well above the 1 kHz capacitive current and the differences' resolution (ngspice prints 12 digits:
about 5e-11 S), so not in cutoff or reverse. And the multiplier's metamorphic relation: every m3 reading is 3 times its
nom reading within 1e-9 relative and 1e-10 absolute (the solver's gmin is not multiplied); a failing row is printed.
Result: the DC law agrees in every region (1e-5 at most, a cutoff current). ngspice-45 has no AC for level 6:
its device table gives no AC load (devices/mos6/mos6init.c:43, `.DEVacLoad = NULL`), and every AC deck aborts with
"doAnalyses: matrix is singular" (exit 1), so its column is refused; VACASK's AC readings are its central differences (2e-10).
Class: an analysis one simulator lacks for a family (no AC, noise or other small-signal analysis on level 6).
Rechecked 2026-11-13 under R91b (../../checked.sh: a run whose exit status is not 0 or whose output says it aborted, stepped too small or met a singular matrix gives refused(<why>), never a reading): every reading reproduced; each ngspice AC deck is refused with its own words.

